1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,540
The lords of the Maya underworld
invited two brothers to a ball game.

2
00:00:04,580 --> 00:00:07,640
It was a trap, and the brothers knew it.

3
00:00:07,660 --> 00:00:09,640
It was how their father had died.

4
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:14,620
The story is told in the Popol Vuh, the
book of the K'iche' Maya of Guatemala.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,160
It was written down in the 1550s,
after the Spanish conquest,

6
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:22,040
and copied by a priest around 1701.

7
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:27,680
The father, Hun Hunahpu, and his
brother played ball so loudly

8
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:31,980
that the lords of Xibalba, the
underworld, heard it overhead.

9
00:00:32,180 --> 00:00:34,400
They sent owls with an invitation.

10
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:38,200
The brothers crossed the
rivers of blood and went down.

11
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:41,460
The lords had set wooden
figures in the seats of honor,

12
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:43,140
and the brothers greeted them.

13
00:00:43,220 --> 00:00:45,260
Then the lords laughed.

14
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:48,700
They offered the brothers
a bench to sit on.

15
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:50,520
It was a burning stone.

16
00:00:50,740 --> 00:00:54,420
They locked them in the House of
Darkness with a torch and a cigar each,

17
00:00:54,420 --> 00:00:57,180
and demanded them back unburned.

18
00:00:57,180 --> 00:00:59,840
By morning, both had burned down.

19
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:03,560
The brothers were sacrificed,
and buried in the ballcourt.

20
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:08,440
Hun Hunahpu's head was hung in a tree,
and the tree began to bear fruit.

21
00:01:08,680 --> 00:01:10,560
A young woman came to look.

22
00:01:10,740 --> 00:01:16,720
The head spat into her hand, and she
conceived twins: Hunahpu and Xbalanque.

23
00:01:16,780 --> 00:01:21,300
They grew up playing ball, and one day
they too made the underworld shake.

24
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:26,300
The same lords sent the same
message: come, and bring your ball.

25
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:29,720
It reached them through a
louse, swallowed by a toad,

26
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:32,860
swallowed by a snake, swallowed by a hawk.

27
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:35,960
Before they left, the
twins planted two canes

28
00:01:35,960 --> 00:01:38,080
in the middle of their
grandmother's house.

29
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:40,640
If the canes dried, they were dead.

30
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:42,960
If they sprouted, they lived.

31
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:45,440
They crossed the rivers on their blowguns.

32
00:01:45,720 --> 00:01:48,520
A mosquito went ahead and
bit each lord in turn.

33
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:51,840
Each cried out, and the next named him.

34
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:56,660
So the twins greeted every lord by
name, and refused the burning bench.

35
00:01:57,060 --> 00:01:58,520
Then came the nights.

36
00:01:58,900 --> 00:02:02,660
In the House of Darkness, they lit
the lords' torch with a macaw's red

37
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:07,580
feathers and their cigars with
fireflies, and returned them unburned.

38
00:02:07,580 --> 00:02:12,440
In the House of Cold they did not freeze,
and the jaguars were thrown bones.

39
00:02:12,720 --> 00:02:16,580
In the House of Bats, Hunahpu
looked out to see if dawn had come,

40
00:02:16,580 --> 00:02:18,560
and a bat cut off his head.

41
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:22,820
His brother called every
animal in the world.

42
00:02:23,060 --> 00:02:25,200
The turtle took the place of the head.

43
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:29,320
In the next ball game, the lords
used the real head as their ball,

44
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:31,580
and Xbalanque set a rabbit loose.

45
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:34,960
While the lords chased it,
he swapped the heads back.

46
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:37,040
But the twins knew their end.

47
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:41,080
They told two soothsayers how to
answer when the lords asked what to do

48
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:45,920
with their bones: grind them like
maize, and scatter them in the river.

49
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:48,040
The lords built an oven.

50
00:02:48,300 --> 00:02:51,560
The twins embraced and
threw themselves in.

51
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:54,120
The lords did as they were told.

52
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:57,300
But the bones sank to
the bottom of the river,

53
00:02:57,340 --> 00:03:00,400
and on the fifth day two fish-men rose.

54
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:04,420
Then two ragged wanderers
appeared and danced.

55
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:07,220
They burned a house and made it whole.

56
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:10,280
They sacrificed each other, and rose.

57
00:03:10,460 --> 00:03:12,280
The lords were delighted.

58
00:03:12,380 --> 00:03:14,640
"Do the same to us," they said.

59
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:17,280
The twins killed the two chief lords,

60
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:21,280
One Death and Seven Death,
and did not bring them back.

61
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:25,700
Then the twins honored their
father, and rose into the sky.

62
00:03:25,980 --> 00:03:29,480
One became the sun, the other the moon.

63
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:32,600
No one knows how old the story is.

64
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:37,740
Maya vases from a thousand years before the
book show figures that may be the twins,

65
00:03:37,740 --> 00:03:41,220
but the book itself was
written after the conquest,

66
00:03:41,340 --> 00:03:44,080
and scholars still argue
about what it kept.

67
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:47,720
Their father lost because
he did not know the tricks.

68
00:03:48,020 --> 00:03:51,440
The twins won because they
had planned their own death.

69
00:03:51,660 --> 00:03:56,360
And the lords of death, it turns
out, could not resist a good show.

70
00:03:56,780 --> 00:04:00,400
A ball, a river and a long way down.

71
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:04,804
If you like old stories from
the people who first told them,

72
00:04:04,804 --> 00:04:07,740
leave a like and subscribe
to Animated Tales.

73
00:04:07,740 --> 00:04:08,607
Until next time.
